  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P1] Restore tenant scoping in the document lookup",
      "body": "Any authenticated user of tenant A can pass a document `id` belonging to tenant B and `findFirst({ where: { id } })` will return that tenant's document instead of `null`. The remaining `ctx.user` check enforces authentication only — ownership is no longer enforced anywhere (after this diff, `tenantId` appears nowhere in `src/`). The removed predicate `tenantId: ctx.user.tenantId` is directly in the diff, so the regression is introduced by this PR and enables cross-tenant reads (IDOR) under realistic inputs. Restore the predicate inside the `where` clause.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/documents.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 33,
        "end": 33
      }
    }
